# Opens TCP port 25 on the Wi-Fi interface so the server can receive mail from
# the internet. Optional: install.sh does not install this file.
#
# It adds a rule to the distribution's existing "inet filter" table and its
# "input" base chain (default policy: drop); it does nothing useful without them.
# The "inet" family covers IPv4 and IPv6, so a host with a global IPv6 address
# accepts SMTP over IPv6 as soon as this is loaded, independently of any IPv4
# port forwarding. IMAP (993) and submission (587/465) are not opened here.
#
# See README.md, "Receiving mail from the internet", for how to load it.
table inet filter {
	chain input {
		iifname "wlan*" tcp dport 25 accept comment "accept SMTP (inbound mail)"
	}
}
